From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] vm: specialize property access and primitive operations

Add bounded weak named and computed property caches, including two-shape
named reads, interned-key reads and writes, and ordinary property-addition
transitions. Trace class and key references, preserve reentrant setters,
check extensibility, and retain generic paths for exotic receivers,
dictionary layouts, accessors and unsupported keys.

Read present ordinary-array storage and guarded numeric typed-array
elements directly. Publish and check their mirrored layouts in the
Static Hermes ABI. String method caches retain slots rather than values
so method replacement and prototype changes preserve existing behavior.

Avoid copying full-range string slices and unchanged ASCII case
conversions. Share JavaScript numeric rounding helpers, add guarded
plain-record and string-operation probes, and retain invocation-owned
string reuse behind the native scope interface. Provide private array
builtins for later guarded callback lowering.

Copy eligible fresh ordinary objects without an own-key array or repeated
shape transitions. Keep descriptor checks and barriered slot writes.
Retain bytecode compatibility rejection and semantic coverage for cache
invalidation, holes, detachment, property effects and native layout checks.
